+        "fbcb31142f279003f13c74101abc9a62": "\nYou are assessing a submitted answer on a given task based on a criterion. Here is the data:\n\n[BEGIN DATA]\n***\n[Task]: Create a UI on surface 'main' for a user settings page. Use a Tabs component with two tabs: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\". The \"Profile\" tab should contain a simple column with a text field for the user's name. The \"# Notifications\" tab should contain a checkbox for \"Enable email notifications\". Also, include a Modal component. The modal's trigger should be a button labeled \"Delete Account\", and its content should be a column with a confirmation text and two buttons: \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\".\n***\n[Submission]: <a2ui-json>\n[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v1.0\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"main\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"basic\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_0\",\n            \"node_5\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_5\",\n          \"component\": \"Modal\",\n          \"trigger\": \"node_6\",\n          \"content\": \"node_8\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_8\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_9\",\n            \"node_10\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_10\",\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_11\",\n            \"node_13\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_13\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"cancel_delete\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"default\",\n          \"child\": \"node_14\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_14\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Cancel\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_11\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"confirm_delete\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"primary\",\n          \"child\": \"node_12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_12\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Confirm Deletion\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_9\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Are you sure you want to delete your account? This action cannot be undone.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_6\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"event\": {\n              \"name\": \"open_modal\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"child\": \"node_7\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_7\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Delete Account\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_0\",\n          \"component\": \"Tabs\",\n          \"tabs\": [\n            {\n              \"title\": \"Profile\",\n              \"child\": \"node_1\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"title\": \"# Notifications\",\n              \"child\": \"node_3\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_3\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_4\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_4\",\n          \"component\": \"CheckBox\",\n          \"label\": \"Enable email notifications\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/notifications/email\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"node_2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"node_2\",\n          \"component\": \"TextField\",\n          \"label\": \"Name\",\n          \"value\": {\n            \"path\": \"/profile/name\"\n          },\n          \"variant\": \"shortText\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dataModel\": {\n        \"profile\": {\n          \"name\": \"Jane Doe\"\n        },\n        \"notifications\": {\n          \"email\": true\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</a2ui-json>\n***\n[Criterion]: The payload should target surfaceId 'main'. The main component should be a Tabs component with 'Profile' and 'Notifications' tabs. The 'Profile' tab should contain a Column with a TextField for 'name', and the 'Notifications' tab should contain a Checkbox for 'Enable email notifications'. A Modal component is also required, triggered by a 'Delete Account' button, containing a Column with confirmation text and 'Confirm Deletion' and 'Cancel' buttons.\n***\n[END DATA]\n\nDoes the submission meet the criterion?\n\n\nAfter assessing the submitted answer, reply with 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.  Please choose ONE option for the grade: either \"C\" for correct answers, \"P\" for partial credit, or \"I\" for incorrect answers.\n\nFor example, after reviewing a correct answer you might write 'GRADE: C' or after reviewing an incorrect answer you might write 'GRADE: I'.\n\nFirst, write out in a step by step manner your reasoning about the criterion to be sure that your conclusion is correct. Avoid simply stating the correct answers at the outset. Then, end with your answer formatted as 'GRADE: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of C, P or I.\n\nNotes for grading:\n1. Variations in capitalization, punctuation, and minor spacing differences should be considered acceptable as long as the semantic intent and required components are present.\n2. Unless a specific vertical or horizontal order is explicitly requested in the task, variations in the order of components within a container should be considered acceptable.\n3. Generated component IDs do not need to match any specific pattern or example in the target, as long as they are unique and correctly establish the requested parent-child relationships.\n4. Minor variations in label text that preserve the core semantic meaning (e.g., 'Submit' vs 'Send', or 'First Name' vs 'Given Name') are acceptable unless exact literal text was requested.\n5. The inclusion of valid optional properties defined in the schema (such as accessibility hints or default values) that were not explicitly requested should not be penalized as long as they make sense in context.\n6. If data binding paths are not explicitly specified in the prompt, accept any logically sound path structure (e.g., accepting `/user/email` or simply `/email` when the prompt asks to \"bind to the user's email\" without specifying a full path).\n7. Partial credit \"P\" can be awarded when the submitted answer is a correct answer with only minor cosmetic variations or additional valid optional properties that do not substantially change the meaning of the component.  When an answer is missing components or contains substantive errors, it should be considered incorrect and awarded an \"I\" grade.\n\n",
+        "7a66dab183684c8990dc1b277ad89b39": "**Assessment of the JSON UI Structure**\n\nOkay, let's break this down. My goal is to rigorously assess this submitted JSON UI structure against a very specific set of requirements. I need to make sure it's up to par with these specifications.\n\nFirst, I see the objective: the target `surfaceId` is \"main\". The structure should have a \"main\" surface. I've got to ensure the entire structure includes a Tabs component as the main component with two tabs: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\". The \"Profile\" tab needs to hold a column, and within that, a text field for the user's name. The \"# Notifications\" tab needs a checkbox for enabling email notifications. Crucially, there's also a Modal component requirement. This modal must be triggered by a \"Delete Account\" button and contain confirmation text and \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\" buttons. This is a pretty standard, but important, UI structure and I need to make sure it is correct.\n\nNow, let's dig into the JSON. Step one: `surfaceId`: I can see `\"createSurface\": { \"surfaceId\": \"main\" ... }`. That's a perfect match, so that box is checked! Then, I look for the root component. It seems to be a Column, with `node_0` (a Tabs component) and `node_5` (a Modal component) inside. Looks good. `node_0` is correctly identified as \"Tabs\", and it has two tabs: \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\". \n\nNext, I look at the contents of the \"Profile\" tab. It appears to be a \"Column\" containing `node_2`, a \"TextField\" labeled \"Name\" (or rather, the text field has a label \"Name\"). The value path for this field, `/profile/name`, looks correct. So far, so good. Then, in the \"# Notifications\" tab, the content is another \"Column\" containing `node_4`, a \"CheckBox\" with the label \"Enable email notifications.\" Excellent. That's another check.\n\nNow, on to the modal component. `node_5` is indeed a \"Modal\", and it has a trigger and content. The trigger, `node_6`, is a \"Button\" labeled \"Delete Account\" (child `node_7` with \"Text\": \"Delete Account\"). Nailed it! The content, `node_8`, looks to be a Column, containing a confirmation text and two buttons. The confirmation text and buttons are nested, but this structure fits the criteria, a column, containing the text, and then a row with the buttons. Great.\n\nI'm now going to confirm my understanding of the step-by-step verification of the prompt. First, is the Surface ID present and is it the right value? Yes, the JSON `\"createSurface\": { \"surfaceId\": \"main\" ... }`. Next, are there tabs: Check, a \"Tabs\" component with titles \"Profile\" and \"# Notifications\" is present. Is the \"Profile\" tab content correct? Yep, a \"Column\" with a `TextField` labeled \"Name\" (or the text field has a label \"Name\"). The \"Notifications\" tab is good as well. And, there's a \"Modal\" component. The trigger is a button labeled \"Delete Account\". Finally, is the content correct? Yep. A `Column` containing confirmation text and two buttons: \"Confirm Deletion\" and \"Cancel\". The buttons are inside a Row which is inside the Column, which meets the \"containing a Column with ...\" portion of the prompt.\n\nSo, after this thorough review, it's clear: The submission perfectly satisfies all the criteria, and everything is implemented as expected. I'm going to give it a \"C\".\n\n\n",
